In article <Dm71TB1w165w@netlink.cts.com>, jdriver@netlink.cts.com (John Driver) writes:
|>         My copy of the spoilers lists a mail daemon as being a 
|> creature in the game.  However, I have never seen one, and when I 
|> try to polymorph into one, the game tells me that it has heard of 
|> no such creature.  Well, why is it listed in the spoilers?  I am 
|> running the dos compile of 3.0j.
|> 
Mail Deamons only appear on multi-tasking computers that have a mail service. 
If you recieve mail while you're playing nethack, a Mail Deamon will run up to
you and give you a scroll of mail.  If you read this scroll, then you will
shell to your mail reader.  This is primarily for unix people who play Nethack
24hrs/day but want to keep at least a thread back to the real world.  :-)


|>         Also, how do you guys keep getting these impossibly low 
|> AC's?  Even with a +3 dragon scale mail your armor class isn't 
|> going to be at -16 like I've seen people posting as theirs.  What's 
|> the secret?

cloaks, shields, boots, etc.  If each are +3, then that adds up quickly.  Also
by donating to a priest, (via #chat) 400*your level in gp, you can get
Protection, which helps your AC.


